    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1045">

                <pb facs="0967" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg653"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor for the Department of
                            State to the German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bernstorff</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of state</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-23">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 23, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: In reply to your note
                    of the 21st instant, with reference to the British S. S. <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mallina</hi>
                     and 
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Tremeadow</hi>, which you state have
                    served as tenders to British cruisers, and are demanding coal in the Panama
                    Canal Zone, I would advise you that these vessels have been considered by the
                    Canal authorities as coming under rule 2 of the President’s proclamation of
                    November 13 last in relation to the neutrality of the Panama Canal Zone,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d1045-f1"/> which <pb facs="0968" n="654" xml:id="pg654"/>
                    accords to transports or fleet auxiliaries the same treatment as that given to
                    belligerent vessels of war.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
